{
  "073049d41b5fbc074175c106f8b1a4ed434beebb4905c360419c3668403843fb": "Create the student table by entering Name in A1, Alice in A2, Brian in A3, and Chloe in A4, and make A1 bold.",
  "077c52cfed3766126a94141a9caaebfbcc2424d7affdbaa7ace7039433c01835": "Split the full names in A2:A5 into first name, middle initial, and last name in columns B:D, using the headers First Name, Middle Initial, and Last Name.",
  "085488dcfa0937f1e487bb65f2863dd067d360b821c766213082d0f33e0d1104": "Create a simple student score table in the spreadsheet. In column A, enter the column header \"Name\" and list three student names below it: Alice, Brian, and Chloe. In column B, enter the column header \"Score\" and list their scores below it: 85, 92, and 78. Make each column header bold",
  "09d824c4ef602641889590fbf867beb0f5029f02899814fbeb8feda6bd938261": "Enter Name, Alice, Brian, and Chloe in A1 through A4, and Department, Math, Science, and English in B1 through B4.",
  "0f33ede5ecae2414275a772193b497bed6416ee0e9e89693b4231efbce5aceab": "Highlight rows 3 and 5 in yellow across columns A through C.",
  "0f34d927e65d948306170a87cc21cbe4454fe1ee86661c90349c2ece4e8246de": "Fill the blank cells in A3 and A5 with \"Unknown\".",
  "12a2ebcf658b3c4aed708a076aa0829f486016c40bdea1c8283ce058e8cf7c71": "Enter Name in A1, Alice in A2, Brian in A3, and Chloe in A4.",
  "1a4fafef80a98be93a426827b57287b6a381df7df6c00e9b35b065903ae8cf7d": "Create the employee table in Sheet1 with Name, Role, and Status headers, enter the listed names, roles, and statuses in A1:C6, and leave A3 and A5 blank.",
  "1b2dc09d17e8ddee5c851318f7016419f1fa3e286d7e23f52e8a5469d4f473b7": "Enter Department in B1, Math in B2, Science in B3, English in B4, Score in C1, 85 in C2, 92 in C3, and 78 in C4.",
  "1d69b12ad09828096687478fe2ec4bf99f048ee2769952e574d073637bc1dc1b": "Create an expense table in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Category\" and list four categories below it: Rent, Meals, Transport, and Supplies. In column B, enter the column header \"Amount\" and list their amounts below it: 1200.123, 45.789, 32.323, and 89.999. Then format the Amount column values as currency with exactly two decimal places.",
  "20bc37a7d5b3af24d3cba6337bec393eb1ea25d2967698f9b6d992a4f4d4320d": "Fill in column C with the header “Middle Initial” and M, T, R, P in C2:C5, and fill in column D with the header “Last Name” and Carter, Lee, Kim, and Jones in D2:D5.",
  "27b826de54cb97cef3d12fbc67925fd5c5e67fe757e2546a69a0f14dc878c6c3": "Create a product sales table in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Product\" and list four products below it: Pen, Notebook, Folder, and Tape. In column B, enter the column header \"Quantity\" and list their quantities below it: 4, 3, 6, and 2. In column C, enter the column header \"Unit Price\" and list their unit prices below it: 1.5, 4.25, 2.1, and 3.75. Then add a column D with the header \"Line Total\" and calculate each line total by multiplying Quantity by Unit Price.",
  "27f6d40a8f61bcb1c521464d17e913d5d3267ab8211558ec7ef875be5f4b1135": "Fill A3 and A5 with \"Unknown\", and enter Engineer, Active, Evan, Intern, and Pending in B5, C5, A6, B6, and C6.",
  "2be6225e3b12f1cf4b955892b066dc65c6bc942ef4f8e9ade81063cee75c3cb6": "Create the product sales table in Sheet1 with the headers and values in A1:D5, and calculate Line Total in D2:D5 as Quantity × Unit Price.",
  "2e98c65cf85b6b76fed351f3f9307f3cb94de7f56f358647ce41fcc270017b6b": "Create a name table in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Full Name\" and list four full names below it: Alice M Carter, Brian T Lee, Chloe R Kim, and David P Jones. Then split each full name into three new columns: column B with the header \"First Name\", column C with the header \"Middle Initial\", and column D with the header \"Last Name\".",
  "306a3c82770f4a5f9f081ba866a8b5784ef215d829738dd1452c9e92492c45b1": "Create the event table in Sheet1 with Event and Date headers, enter Kickoff, Review, Launch, and Wrap-up with the four date texts, then convert the Date values to actual dates and format them as yyyy-MM-dd.",
  "31bb55b9e60da265509ea98338e3dc4bbdc87b20876f877b0f8810438efac7ce": "Add the Tax Amount column in D1:D4, with Tax Amount in D1 and 16, 6, and 2 in D2:D4.",
  "3306d14ad2d32a403439a66191a0586c9843e2e765de4171ec6c4f1ab5ff71cd": "Create the name table in Sheet1 with the Full Name list in A1:A5, then split each name into First Name in B1:B5, Middle Initial in C1:C5, and Last Name in D1:D5.",
  "3553c029f4f66f5f9c978129f946a8818dfe3c08e18e095c2dcb60cc30817055": "Enter Category in A1, then enter Rent, Meals, Transport, and Supplies in A2 through A5.",
  "399f0f57ebd0b2a56047e24fba4b3ac956fcc7b35b3358d52913d6073bda67aa": "Create the inventory table in Sheet1 with the specified headers and product, inventory, and reorder level values in A1:C6, then highlight the entire rows for Marker and Eraser in yellow.",
  "440c95165a634dfd66f12b7c580edf6d677730f375470716492ebcd4b2c411db": "Enter Product, Quantity, and Unit Price in A1:C1, then enter Pen, 4, and 1.5 in row 2; Notebook, 3, and 4.25 in row 3; Folder, 6, and 2.1 in row 4; and Tape, 2, and 3.75 in row 5.",
  "4eecf8edf87ebced60d723ba900027aabc5029dab03b4b1061e21981c75f90aa": "Enter the Department and Score columns in B1:C4, and make A1:A4 red.",
  "4fca5ff139907f7221b61308b6cbea25af592494d5229ff53c13a19596756ca5": "Enter Email in B1 and alice@google.com, brian@google.com, alice@google.com, chloe@google.com, and brian@google.com in B2 through B6.",
  "54cb6be1134710fb291ef2b7e6b9ed08bdd9b59242de420de531f055e408b987": "Enter Middle Initial in C1 and M, T, R, and P in C2 through C5.",
  "559cb565f5abc635a41b721c45f7a06023a274c89dd55dae8a5ea6abf1422ab6": "Enter Tax Amount in D1, calculate Amount × Tax Rate in D2:D4, enter Final Amount in E1, and calculate Amount + Tax Amount in E2:E4.",
  "5ba3ab5cb76ee2c59518b2934ce9d7bcebfe4ab190a2f0a1dfa4ffa0352e7d8f": "Enter Full Name in A1 and Alice M Carter, Brian T Lee, Chloe R Kim, and David P Jones in A2 through A5.",
  "61c7f4d1764370902144d073b1949f7b11ecf8f9df246073409f66f2a1ec8acc": "Create the phone list in Sheet1 with the headers and names in columns A and B, and format the phone numbers in B2:B5 as ###-###-####.",
  "6563edb3802313c841bebeee02dad3f10561b3e10b23b1503229376602e7e49e": "Create the table in Sheet1 with Name, Department, and Score in A1:C1, then enter Alice, Brian, and Chloe in A2:A4, Math, Science, and English in B2:B4, and 85, 92, and 78 in C2:C4.",
  "6941ee3b407b91ae784dcfd3b4f3d9c2492fa725b5804882ca6fce8ba70f3d3c": "Create the expense table in Sheet1 by entering Category in A1, Rent/Meals/Transport/Supplies in A2:A5, and Amount in B1 with 1200.123, 45.789, 32.323, and 89.999 in B2:B5.",
  "6df6f908e5b6a65aab2d09bcf56399a435ffe5737256d6f1e81b258f1d3201bc": "Enter Amount in B1 and 1200.123, 45.789, 32.323, and 89.999 in B2 through B5.",
  "6f8358e2d9f7815976073430cb2dc56c3a31bebf153a68bebade45cae3bb561e": "Format B2:B5 as dates with the yyyy-MM-dd number format.",
  "72a57a12429e625d3195f0deb617c6f8484e0935656a0ba31d037ef160c967a8": "Create the student score table by entering Name in A1 and Score in B1, listing Alice, Brian, and Chloe in A2:A4 and 85, 92, and 78 in B2:B4, and make A1 and B1 bold.",
  "7bc9564b5e97cbb0a05b87a6b5fd5ecd0660f16ccff5b8bc4f96f5b8b3dbf80c": "No changes are needed.",
  "8105fe831e1416088d53b06199d948ed986ded65faab294ad63611933b175991": "Create the contact table in Sheet1 with the Name and Email columns, fill in the five names and emails, and bold the duplicate email values in column B.",
  "8670010409ed3dce14389494a2ee5d894024ff4ba677bc6b9242482bc64bab4a": "Create an inventory table in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Product\" and list five products below it: Pencil, Marker, Notebook, Eraser, and Folder. In column B, enter the column header \"Inventory\" and list the inventory values below it: 25, 8, 12, 4, and 30. In column C, enter the column header \"Reorder Level\" and list the reorder levels below it: 20, 15, 10, 8, and 25. Then highlight the entire row in yellow for each product where Inventory is less than Reorder Level.",
  "8d5f606d59bcff5685b5561630428995346a51f8b673ab20902258bf4a5068f6": "Create the employee table in Sheet1 with Name, Role, and Status headers, enter Alice, Manager, Active; Unknown, Analyst, Active; Chloe, Designer, Leave; Unknown, Engineer, Active; and Evan, Intern, Pending in rows 2–6.",
  "92ad8a867462cccc0e46a499a811c26849ff48fd299816088792eac0dd844470": "Create an employee table in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Name\". Enter Alice in A2, leave A3 blank, enter Chloe in A4, leave A5 blank, and enter Evan in A6. In column B, enter the column header \"Role\" and list the roles below it: Manager, Analyst, Designer, Engineer, and Intern. In column C, enter the column header \"Status\" and list the statuses below it: Active, Active, Leave, Active, and Pending. Then fill every blank cell in column A within A2:A6 with \"Unknown\".",
  "92cfa4f82eadd95eabda3790baf122e16d59acc85f4c01f83bcf3ad417e1e8ac": "Make cells A1 through A4 red.",
  "98a037c483d0df5b07498c5cd9ceaeaed8db76e5cd6dda6d72daa12c8c7b05aa": "Normalize the phone numbers in B2:B4 to the ###-###-#### format.",
  "9946686f693b9961ee12193fe1e96edaf3c30223fabb9e8087cb6afcef87778a": "Enter the remaining values in row 5 and row 6: leave A5 blank, enter Engineer in B5, Active in C5, Evan in A6, Intern in B6, and Pending in C6.",
  "a06b4aa37b5b1f5966bb1013a5a445100d12b0703aad20ddd188ae02c7093bdd": "Create the invoice table in Sheet1 with headers Item, Amount, Tax Rate, Tax Amount, and Final Amount, and enter Desk, Chair, and Lamp with their amounts, tax rates, tax amounts, and final amounts.",
  "a1b48b67725bbb9d533761e30bf7a30050baab9a737c8af4d1ce3f8c270c0df7": "Enter Score in B1, enter 85, 92, and 78 in B2 through B4, and make B1 bold.",
  "a782697356dc76340cc852052f11c8d3153203dd3c8d1aa32b56b1e9c4de8b07": "Create the name table in Sheet1 with Full Name in A1, Alice M Carter through David P Jones in A2:A5, and First Name in B1 with Alice, Brian, Chloe, and David in B2:B5.",
  "a9511e733c440819f58bb831f21d65034901f662fb736183e2ecd11eda2db700": "Create the inventory table in Sheet1 and highlight the rows for Marker and Eraser in yellow.",
  "aa9d50caf9d7bb0f1c418ef21d545eabdbc67096d3cb457c4df67f433d217abf": "Create a phone list in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Name\" and list four names below it: Alice, Brian, Chloe, and Daniel. In column B, enter the column header \"Phone Number\" and list their phone numbers below it: (415) 555 0182, 212.555.0198, 6175550134, and 305-555-0177. Then normalize every phone number in column B into the ###-###-#### format.",
  "b26b884981eeff947e5bbb830d7ad6a1c370ecb8442ab03a2ac711b114ecaac4": "Enter Department in B1, Math in B2, Science in B3, and English in B4.",
  "b413e9d7640746e3b77109e7eb78f5cd0f2303f726e8de2d1b229d8cb301d8cf": "Split the full names in column A into columns B and C by entering the headers First Name and Middle Initial, then fill B2:B5 with Alice, Brian, Chloe, and David and C2:C5 with M, T, R, and P.",
  "b5d4ebc195cdc0ea4253cadeaa1736c289d9eba8322f5b332439932ef4f5922c": "Create an event date table in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Event\" and list four events below it: Kickoff, Review, Launch, and Wrap-up. In column B, enter the column header \"Date\" and list the date text below it: Jan 5, 2024; Feb 14, 2024; Mar 3, 2024; and Apr 22, 2024. Then convert the Date column values into actual date values and format them as yyyy-MM-dd.",
  "b6a7d63636b60bfa045a379ad90aa6c4dc73971561de2b11f22cef77e64c2954": "Create the contact table in Sheet1 by entering Name in A1, Alice through Emma in A2:A6, Email in B1, and the listed email addresses in B2:B6.",
  "b732ae2759668a9bb08c822fa99080910973e8830c27e025bcd8e34e7725202b": "Enter Analyst in B3, Active in C3, Chloe in A4, Designer in B4, Leave in C4, Engineer in B5, Active in C5, Evan in A6, Intern in B6, and Pending in C6, leaving A3 and A5 blank.",
  "b8d42ee7d42d3ac9a2c93bc8148d2cc6db7bd23973f325d1072eada8a9f9e1c0": "Create the contact table in Sheet1 by entering Name in A1 and Alice, Brian, Chloe, Daniel, and Emma in A2:A6.",
  "bc60d8a6fbda98ae42d72cd85e4d95a22200ecead0224337fa079acf194ec0bb": "Enter First Name in B1 and Alice, Brian, Chloe, and David in B2 through B5.",
  "bec165744650594d6430884eaff7c69afa4b15b2cceb1a1afe2aa1756ad9fee1": "Enter Name in A1 and make A1 bold.",
  "c040902d1709da85de8d97cd63130442e357af61ae4895e5a9d8ed0844253003": "In Sheet1, create the table with Name, Department, and Score in A1:C4 using Alice, Brian, Chloe; Math, Science, English; and 85, 92, 78, then make A1:A4 red.",
  "c2fd2a213d2534858349b7939d1e6d721fd8d134d1fa5a0c009a550702661903": "Create the expense table in Sheet1 with Category in A1, Rent/Meals/Transport/Supplies in A2:A5, Amount in B1, 1200.123/45.789/32.323/89.999 in B2:B5, and format B2:B5 as currency with exactly two decimal places.",
  "c5c7c9312d27bd1889e96c91d7ae3948dd74408ea2f4773086c10e8829bae5f4": "Fill column D with the header Last Name in D1 and Carter, Lee, Kim, and Jones in D2:D5.",
  "c8a7b261c1cfae5e2553a3beec9bd7140229b0bf3009e035f10e361ff6063cc6": "Add a Line Total column in D1:D5 and calculate the totals for each product.",
  "cccb86a3bb529e9783d552a7ed0c536be5eac1d3ab795894026fbe7729b40eca": "Create the event date table in Sheet1 with Event and Date headers, list Kickoff, Review, Launch, and Wrap-up with their dates, and convert the Date column values to actual dates formatted as yyyy-MM-dd.",
  "d7f1c0f03e28af57a1212c5d01f0dfad5f07b193993017593f8572743d81b1f8": "Create the invoice table in Sheet1 with Item, Amount, and Tax Rate in A1:C1; Desk, Chair, and Lamp with amounts 200, 75, and 40 and tax rates 0.08, 0.08, and 0.05 in rows 2–4; and add Tax Amount in D1 with 16, 6, and 2 in D2:D4.",
  "d95802f2927f0cc071dcb0326a52887d238d7a1763e6a05befa8bdb875d40d5b": "Add the Final Amount column in E1:E4 with Final Amount in E1 and values 216, 81, and 42 in E2:E4.",
  "dc50f23f0b1b55a6e846937da34c0ab0c25f9a752b325e9a1e69c420875798ac": "Format the Amount values in B2:B5 as currency with exactly two decimal places.",
  "dc69cbafb3763eb7c0355805daa1c24673fc82323d7b7a49bcd9318d1cb25c6b": "In Sheet1, create a simple table with headers Name, Department, and Score in the first row. The names are 'Alice', 'Brian', 'Chole'. The departments are 'Math', 'Science', 'English'. The scores are 85, 92, 78. Then make the first column red",
  "e098b3b96a676733fa96498c842fecabeda0ec7c88bd6a36575db8cae3d6ebea": "Enter Alice, Brian, and Chloe in A2 through A4.",
  "e1dd225470f3c6224e2b4c9d0769e037b29b6a955138274c88e422a72ab8055c": "Enter the Email column values in B1:B6 and bold the duplicate email entries in B2, B3, B4, and B6.",
  "e38d07643b29b8df8c210658526e35a750414ca40f90e1cdd6d58895565701c7": "Enter Analyst and Active in B3 and C3, and enter Chloe, Designer, and Leave in A4:C4.",
  "e3e44589e9a23b9ea7dd4ceed4b3931252a67f968805d6849d51a4282ba082b6": "Enter Amount in B1, enter 1200.123, 45.789, 32.323, and 89.999 in B2 through B5, and format B2:B5 as currency with two decimal places.",
  "e414c5d5780057c87bf7214f27fc9ee762b1a848c9f1c116a705580e812028bc": "Enter Unknown, Chloe, Unknown, and Evan in A3 through A6, and enter Analyst, Designer, Engineer, and Intern in B3 through B6 along with Active, Leave, Active, and Pending in C3 through C6.",
  "e5102c84a0f24263f49a593f0abe73a05117d85f78743191ba21ef37e67a3f1b": "Enter Name in A1, Role in B1, Status in C1, Alice in A2, Manager in B2, and Active in C2.",
  "e9b8939e6cd2319eb7d7233804daf6f7544771e533a4e0bef7c1a1eeb9821cce": "Create a contact table in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Name\" and list five names below it: Alice, Brian, Chloe, Daniel, and Emma. In column B, enter the column header \"Email\" and list their emails below it: alice@google.com, brian@google.com, alice@google.com, chloe@google.com, and brian@google.com. Then apply conditional formatting to the Email column so duplicate email values are bolded.",
  "ea04c6488dc8c0ac6fad9791618c8cc81e62d16e4bf4b4cad46ab9145d3c6a4c": "Create an invoice table in Sheet1. In column A, enter the column header \"Item\" and list three items below it: Desk, Chair, and Lamp. In column B, enter the column header \"Amount\" and list their amounts below it: 200, 75, and 40. In column C, enter the column header \"Tax Rate\" and list their tax rates below it: 0.08, 0.08, and 0.05. Then add column D with the header \"Tax Amount\" and calculate Amount multiplied by Tax Rate. Add column E with the header \"Final Amount\" and calculate Amount plus Tax Amount.",
  "eb45e6cba8d41d5bfb52265b6ddd6e2de447a3629f054064629bc2ef9eab2df1": "Create the phone list in Sheet1 by entering Name in A1, Phone Number in B1, Alice through Daniel in A2:A5, and the listed phone numbers in B2:B5.",
  "f3eda28a95d2b5b7d38019de01c45993fe89dc567d111bd9f317d986bb3d9d02": "Enter the Score header and scores 85, 92, and 78 in column C, then make A1:A4 red.",
  "f5d67ee8adc64e22c9d31462b382c18ef94bc3d73b66795fced21d5908c0f3a3": "Enter Score in C1 and 85, 92, and 78 in C2 through C4.",
  "f6a7dde3f2c6b5b4e4f87038f8806d6bd725d1146023a36016ff6ef7016890ef": "Enter Alice, Brian, and Chloe in A2 through A4, and enter Score in B1 with 85, 92, and 78 in B2 through B4.",
  "fc2034caf40c8d1117997123c8f60a2e33ce9b66b1a7bc3b449eb1067f08f0ae": "Make the duplicate email values in B2, B3, B4, and B6 bold.",
  "fef92c640effe66b3eed7db06aa07cbb3444a3a620426a45e799cef65a26a612": "Create the employee table in Sheet1 with Name, Role, and Status headers; enter Alice, Manager, and Active in row 2; leave A3 blank; enter Analyst and Active in row 3; enter Chloe, Designer, and Leave in row 4.",
  "ff7ef143548c1252beab0b76cb8198d735a713d3a342808599530f4c5a14f306": "Create the name table in Sheet1 by entering the full names in A1:A5 and splitting them into First Name in B1:B5 and Middle Initial in C1:C5."
}
